When a player or enemy deals [[damage]] to their targets' [[health]] or [[shields]], that damage may be mitigated by sources of '''damage reduction''' (also called '''damage resistance''' relative to receiving damage). In other words, players may deal less damage than the listed [[Arsenal]] value due to [[armor]]; damage type modifiers from different health, armor, and shield classes; and/or other sources of damage reduction.

Note that in-game and on the wiki, sometimes [[Abilities]] and [[Mod]] descriptions mention damage reduction when they really mean ''negative [[Damage Type Modifier|damage type modifier]]'' and vice versa. This distinction is needed to differentiate between [[Calculating Bonuses|multiplicative and additive stacking]] of different forms of damage reduction.
{{tocright|limit=3}}
==How Damage Reduction Affects Damage==
{{Main|Damage/Calculation}}
===Basic===
When a player is dealt damage, it is reduced by a scalar calculated from the amount of damage reduction (DR) active (from [[Mod]]s, Warframe [[abilities]], etc.). The general calculation takes a form of:
:<math>
\begin{aligned}
\text{Damage Received} &= \text{Damage Dealt} \times (1 - \text{DR}_{1}) \times (1 - \text{DR}_{2}) \times \cdots \\
&= \text{Damage Dealt} \times \text{Total Damage Multiplier}
\end{aligned}
</math>

For example, if a Grineer {{E|Lancer}} normally deals 100 IPS damage (50 {{D|Impact}}, 25 {{D|Puncture}}, and 25 {{D|Slash}}) against a player, and that damage is dealt to the player's shields, which have an innate 50% DR, the amount of damage the player receives will be:
:{{Math|({{D|Impact|50}} + {{D|Puncture|25}} + {{D|Slash|25}}) {{mul}} (1 - 50%)|mt=y}}

===With Armor===
In the case of [[Armor|armored]] targets (players and enemies), the modified damage dealt is calculated as:
:<math>
\begin{aligned}
\text{Damage Received} &= \text{Damage Dealt} \times (1 - \text{DR}_{1}) \times (1 - \text{DR}_{2}) \times \cdots \times \frac{300}{300 + \text{Armor}} \\
&= \text{Damage Dealt} \times \text{Total Damage Multiplier from Pure Damage Reduction} \times \text{Total Damage Multiplier from Armor}
\end{aligned}
</math>

For example, if 100 pure {{D|Impact}} damage is dealt to a player with 500 armor, the amount of damage they receive will be:
:{{Math|{{D|Impact|100}} {{mul}} 300/(300 + 500)|mt=y}}

===With Damage Type Modifiers and Physical/Elemental Damage===
[[Damage Type Modifier]]s (DM, not to be confused with damage ''reduction'', DR) play a role in damage calculations. Although the {{D|Tenno}} are neutral to all damage types as of {{ver|27.2}}, mods such as {{M|Toxin Resistance}} or ability effects like {{A|Kinetic Plating}} add damage modifiers to a player's health and shields against either one type of damage:
*{{D|Toxin}} for {{M|Toxin Resistance}}
*or multiple ({{D|Impact}}, {{D|Puncture}}, {{D|Slash}}, {{D|Heat}}, {{D|Cold}}, and {{D|Blast}} for {{A|Kinetic Plating}}.

The generalized formula from above can be modified to account for these as such:
:<math>
\begin{aligned}
\text{Damage Type Received} &= \text{Damage Type Dealt} \times (1 - \text{DR}_{1}) \times (1 - \text{DR}_{2}) \times \cdots \times \frac{300}{300 + \text{Armor}} \times (1 + \text{DM}_{1}) \times (1  + \text{DM}_{2}) \times \cdots \\
&= \text{Damage Type Dealt} \times \text{Total Damage Multiplier from Pure Damage Reduction} \times \text{Total Damage Multiplier from Armor} \times \text{Total Damage Multiplier from Damage Type Modifiers}
\end{aligned}
</math>

For example, if 50 {{D|Impact}}, 25 {{D|Puncture}}, and 25 {{D|Slash}} damage is dealt to {{D|Corpus}} health, with 100 armor, and [[Guardian Eximus]] aura active (90% DR), the amount of damage the enemy receives will be:
:{{Math|{{D|Impact|50}} {{mul}} (1 - 90%) {{mul}} (1 - 100/(100 + 300)) {{mul}} (1 + {{D|Corpus|0%}})|mt=y}}
:{{Math|{{D|Puncture|25}} {{mul}} (1 - 90%) {{mul}} (1 - 100/(100 + 300)) {{mul}} (1 + {{D|Corpus|50%}})|mt=y}}
:{{Math|{{D|Slash|25}} {{mul}} (1 - 90%) {{mul}} (1 - 100/(100 + 300)) {{mul}} (1 + {{D|Corpus|0%}})|mt=y}}

===Against Non-Health/Shield Types===
Damage Reduction has no affect on effects that absorb damage, {{D|Overguard}}, or {{D|Object}} health such as:
*{{WF|Frost}}'s {{A|Snow Globe}} and {{M|Icy Avalanche}}
*{{WF|Nezha}}'s {{A|Warding Halo}} (during 3-second invulnerability period; DR to health after 3-second period works normally) 
*{{WF|Rhino}}'s {{A|Iron Skin}}
*{{WF|Saryn}}'s {{A|Molt}}

Some of these may ''benefit'' from increased Armor (e.g. damage absorption scales with Armor values), but Damage Reduction will not be applied to these to reduce incoming damage received.

